# Ganbare Goemon: Toukai Douchuu Ooedo Tengurigaeshi no Maki (NDS), the glyphs of ssfont.dat.
# KEY is the glyph index in ssssf.dat (000-5DB) as three hex digits, the value the character it draws.
# Read by eye from renders of every glyph, then checked against the furigana in the ss_*.dat scripts
# (every kanji with a reading was compared with it) and by reading decoded lines. Glyphs no script
# uses were read from the image alone. Half-width (8-pixel) glyphs map to ASCII, full-width ones to
# full-width characters. 2FC, the half-width space, is given by the adapter itself (HALF_SPACE), since
# a line that ends in a space does not survive every editor.
# 466-468 are the vertical forms of ー, 「 and 」 used in vertically set text.
# Not in the table: 35D (unidentified), and three duplicates noted below.
